[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3401276697","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111634#issuecomment-3401276697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111634","id":3401276697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ku10Z","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T11:09:01Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T11:09:01Z","body":"I'd say an iterative approach should only be adopted if it doesn't add any significant overhead to reasonably complex cases, unless things break down at reasonably low scales\n\nI don't expect `match` to break down for any reasonably scaled input, but if it can be repeated in non-destructive testing or non-toy cases then that's something to check\n\nWe could also just add an artificial limit like some other recursive methods have","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3401276697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3401297317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111634#issuecomment-3401297317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111634","id":3401297317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ku62l","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T11:15:40Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T11:15:40Z","body":"Please note that even if we eliminate the stack overflow crash (by replacing recursion with a loop) and optimize away consecutive wildcards (as far as I understand, `***...*` is equivalent to `*`), in general we still can't avoid freezing for long input strings and/or patterns with a large number of wildcards due to \"catastrophic backtracking\", which also exists in regular expressions.\n\nThe example you demonstrated is likely beyond its intended use (there's no point in repeating the wildcard `*` multiple times in a row). Perhaps we should just document this?","author_a